    "text": "Let the lengths of intercepts on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> -axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> -axis made by the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>, respectively. Then the shortest distance from origin to a tangent to this circle which is perpendicular to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> is equal to :"
  },
